.TH CALLOC 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
calloc \- allocate zero-initialized memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdlib.h>
.PP
.BI "void* calloc(size_t " count ", size_t " size ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR calloc ()
allocates a block for
.I count
objects of
.I size
bytes and initializes all bytes to zero.
Release the returned pointer with
.BR free (3crunch).
A zero-size request attempts an allocation and can return a freeable pointer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, returns a nonnull pointer. On failure, returns null and sets
.BR errno .
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOMEM
The product overflows, the size is too large, or memory could not be obtained.
.SH NOTES
The allocator is not thread-safe, and Crunch
.B errno
is process-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR malloc (3crunch),
.BR free (3crunch),
.BR realloc (3crunch)
